---
layout: null
search: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Search index for the caravan site.

  Regenerated by Jekyll on every build, so it always matches the live content —
  there is nothing to maintain by hand. Edit a page, run ./deploy.sh, done.

  What lands in here:
    - every page and article whose front matter has `search: true`
      (that is the default; see the `defaults:` block in _config.yml)
    - a page opts out with `search: false`
    - content excluded in _config.yml never gets built at all, so it can
      never reach this file

  Liquid's strip_html removes <script> and <style> blocks before the tags,
  so inline CSS and JavaScript stay out of the index. That does mean any
  content generated by JavaScript at runtime — the itinerary's day-by-day
  cards, for instance — is invisible here. Those pages carry a
  `search_summary` in their front matter to compensate.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Filter is `!= false`, not `== true`, deliberately. A page opts OUT explicitly;
  anything else is indexed. If the `defaults:` block in _config.yml ever stops
  applying, pages stay searchable rather than silently vanishing from results.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign indexed_pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.search != false" -%}
{%- assign indexed_articles = site.articles | where_exp: "a", "a.search != false" -%}
{%- assign entries = indexed_pages | concat: indexed_articles -%}
[
{%- for item in entries %}
  {
    "id": {{ forloop.index0 }},
    "title": {{ item.title | default: "Untitled" | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ item.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
    "kind": {% if item.collection == "articles" %}"Journal"{% else %}"Page"{% endif %},
    "summary": {{ item.search_summary | default: item.hero_sub | default: item.summary | default: "" | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "body": {{ item.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncatewords: 700 | jsonify }}
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
]
